flowchart TD
  Registry["lang/__init__.py adapter_for(lang) / has_adapter(lang)"]
  Base["lang/base.py LanguageAdapter (chunk, symbols, import_refs, resolve) + SymbolTable"]
  TS["lang/treesitter.py get_parser/parse/chunk_tree -- grammar-driven chunking shared by all adapters"]

  Registry --> CSharp["csharp.py CSharpAdapter"]
  Registry --> TypeScript["typescript.py TypeScriptAdapter (also registered for 'javascript')"]
  Registry --> Python["python_lang.py PythonAdapter"]
  Registry --> Go["golang.py GoAdapter"]
  Registry --> Fallback["fallback.py FallbackAdapter -- window-chunking, used when has_adapter() is false"]

  Base -.implements.-> CSharp
  Base -.implements.-> TypeScript
  Base -.implements.-> Python
  Base -.implements.-> Go
  TS --> CSharp
  TS --> TypeScript
  TS --> Python
  TS --> Go

  CSharp --> CSGotcha["gotcha: block namespaces need explicit walk (probe_grammar.py first)"]
  TypeScript --> TSGotcha["gotcha: export_statement wraps the real declaration node"]
  Python --> PyGotcha["gotcha: decorated_definition wraps def/class when decorators are present"]

  CSharp -.resolve via.-> UsingTarget["_using_target() -> namespace-declaring files (index/edges.py same-namespace edges)"]
  TypeScript -.resolve via.-> Candidates["_candidates()/_join() -> relative import resolution"]
  Python -.resolve via.-> ModuleFiles["_module_files()/_relative_base() -> dotted import resolution"]
  Go -.resolve via.-> PkgFanout["module-qualified import -> package directory (fanout capped)"]

  Rule["CLAUDE.md ground rule: pin grammar node types empirically via scripts/probe_grammar.py against a fixture before writing a chunker"] -.-> TS
